@node "A500" "My new pet !"
@{JCENTER}@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/32seonliner.png"}


You found a hidden gem ;)




Part II "NEW Amiga 500"


My aim is one computer for all and it's a mATX build and in
a simple way to bring more Amiga feeling to it.


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/640-1.jpeg"}
(sorry for the all crap around my desk ha ha ha)


Last time I put some stickers to make it more a Amiga and less
whatever it was before ;)


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/640-2.jpeg"}

The build is still work in progress, I'm still debating on the
slim DVD attached under the case between the 2 front legs and 
put a CD32 sticker on it so I can do real emulation of the 
mighty Commodore Amiga CD32 ...

Now this time I have added 2 DB9 joystick ports, games on Amiga
should be played with a joystick, it feels wrong with a gamepad
on many games, I remeber on my CD32 I had back in the 90s I had
to plug my Tac 2 for some games if not most of them because the
pad was not that great. 


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/2joyadapter.png"}


I bought a USB-C joystick adapter way ago and at that time I was
aiming at a Mac mini build that felt just impossible to make a
nice build off so I trashed the idea for atleast a year ago.


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/alinea.png"}


I bought it from Alinea, there is a ready internal version but 
I'm not to throw out money because of this so I stick to what I 
have, the external USB-C version.


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/500-1.jpeg"}


2 Commodore joystick ports ;)



@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/500-4.jpeg"}


It would look alot better with a internal version ...



@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/500-2.jpeg"}
@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/500-3.jpeg"}


Not the greatest joystick but it works!
This is a replica of the classic Atari joystick that was crap,
it had thin plastick cross that easily broke if you where
too hard pushing it on directions.

This has a more robust if not too robust construction with
microswitches, I hate that clicky noice otherwise a very nice
joystick, It's like the crap that comes nowdays with THE64,
It's so annoying noice, it removes the pleasure of gaming.
Maybe I can replace the switches with silent one if there is
such microswitches to buy.


This is it ... now I'm to enjoy my A500 a bit and think about 
the DVD unit and do some testing if it's even worth having
one mounted ... maybe there will be a part III in future


I have one final tought on the PC build itself, I'm surprised
on the noice level, it never above slighty fan breeze at max.
Something like 27db at Amiga emulation to less than 40db in 
AAA PC games. It's very quiet that's what I'm trying to
explain, maybe the fan blades itself is next level ??
It has to be quiet in the room before I notice theres actually
a fan spinning ... This is ofcource my luck to have bought
quality stuff ;)


Thanks for reading hope my build gives you some great ideas!



@{FG shine}
*** ***
*********
**** ****
*******
*****
*
@{FG text}


@{JLEFT}
@endnode 




@node "AB" "Alien Breed 35th Anniversary Collection"
@{JCENTER}@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/32seonliner.png"}

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/ab.jpg"}

THE BREED IS BACK! Celebrate 35 years of Alien Breed with the 
definitive collection.
 
Featuring 6 classic games, interactive archives, modern 
controls, visual enhancements, co-op multiplayer, Online 
Rush Mode and Horde Mode, bringing the complete sci-fi 
horror legacy back to your screens.

This collection won't run on any Amiga, it's for modern
platforms like consoles, PCs.

Yeahh this can't be missed out, this is alot of fun ;)


